      <div class="mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buyers Make</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Incline machines are specialist equipment, and these four mistakes turn a specialist purchase into a general-purpose disappointment.</p>
        <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying steep incline you will not use</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 40% grade range costs real money. If most of your sessions are flat, a conventional treadmill gives you a better deck and console for the same budget.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ignoring ceiling height at maximum grade</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Your head sits far higher at 40% than at flat. Measure clearance with your tallest user standing on the deck at full incline.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming automatic grade control is included</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Manual incline always works. Automatic terrain matching is subscription content on the machines that offer it, and it is usually the reason people want one.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Neglecting the lift motor</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Frequent steep work loads the incline mechanism heavily. It needs its own attention in the maintenance routine, not just the belt.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
